@page "/docs/theming/color-scheme"

@* Light and dark: the app's default, the reader's choice (ColorSchemeSwitch and the ib-scheme
   cookie), a scheme for part of a page, and your own colors in both. From docs/styling.md
   ("Tokens", "A color scheme for part of a page") and components.md (ColorSchemeSwitch). *@

<ArticlePage Section="theming" Slug="color-scheme">
    <Lead>
        Every color comes in a light and a dark version. Pages follow the device's setting until your app or your reader
        picks one, and any part of a page can have its own scheme.
    </Lead>
    <ChildContent>
        <Heading Level="2">The app's default</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            Use <Code>ColorScheme</Code> on the <Code>IzzyTheme</Code> in the <Code>head</Code>: <Code>Auto</Code> (the
            default) follows the device, and <Code>Light</Code> or <Code>Dark</Code> holds one until the reader picks another.
        </TextBlock>
        <Code Block Language="razor">@Default</Code>
        <TextBlock>
            In plain HTML, <Code>data-ib-color-scheme="light"</Code> or <Code>"dark"</Code> on the <Code>html</Code> element
            holds one too, but it also overrides the reader's choice below, so use <Code>IzzyTheme</Code> when readers can pick.
        </TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">Let readers choose</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            Use <Anchor Href="docs/components/color-scheme-switch">ColorSchemeSwitch</Anchor>: a menu of System, Light and
            Dark for headers, a light/dark toggle, or all three side by side for a settings page.
        </TextBlock>
        <ExampleViewer Example="color-scheme-switch-variants" />
        <TextBlock>
            The choice is kept in the <Code>ib-scheme</Code> cookie. The <Code>IzzyTheme</Code> in the <Code>head</Code> reads
            it on the server, so pages arrive in the reader's scheme with no flash: keep one there, even an empty
            <Code>&lt;IzzyTheme /&gt;</Code>. Reading the cookie takes <Code>AddIzzyBlazor()</Code>.
        </TextBlock>
        <TextBlock>
            With JavaScript off, each option is a link to an endpoint that <Code>MapIzzyBlazor()</Code> adds. It saves the
            cookie and sends the reader back.
        </TextBlock>
        <Code Block Language="csharp">@Services</Code>
        <TextBlock>
            On an interactive page, <Code>@@bind-Value</Code> gives you the choice as a <Code>ColorScheme</Code>:
            <Code>Auto</Code> for System, <Code>Light</Code> or <Code>Dark</Code>.
        </TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">A scheme for part of a page</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            Use <Code>ColorScheme</Code> on <Code>Box</Code>, <Code>Stack</Code>, <Code>Card</Code> and the other layout
            components, or a part of the <Anchor Href="docs/components/app-shell">app layout</Anchor>: <Code>Dark</Code>
            for a dark sidebar or header in a light app, <Code>Light</Code>, or <Code>Inverse</Code> for the opposite of the
            page, even when the page follows the device.
        </TextBlock>
        <ExampleViewer Example="box-scheme" />
        <TextBlock>
            Every color switches inside it, so text, links, buttons, badges, fields, focus rings and menus opened from it keep
            their contrast. <Code>Bg</Code> still applies on top: <Code>Bg="Color.Fill"</Code> is that scheme's
            container shade. On your own elements, <Code>data-ib-color-scheme="dark"</Code>, <Code>"light"</Code> or
            <Code>"inverse"</Code> does the same.
        </TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">Your colors in both schemes</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            Write a color as a <Code>light-dark()</Code> pair and one value covers both schemes, including parts of a page
            with their own:
        </TextBlock>
        <Code Block Language="css">@LightDark</Code>
        <TextBlock>
            Give a color the same value twice, or a plain color, if it shouldn't change with the scheme. Keep text at 4.5:1
            on what it sits on in both.
        </TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">Next steps</Heading>
        <List Gap="2">
            <ListItem><Anchor Href="docs/theming/tokens">Tokens and customizing</Anchor>: every color as a CSS variable.</ListItem>
            <ListItem><Anchor Href="docs/components/color-scheme-switch">ColorSchemeSwitch</Anchor>: the full API.</ListItem>
        </List>
    </ChildContent>
</ArticlePage>

@code {
    private const string Default = """
        <IzzyTheme Preset="ThemePreset.Standard" ColorScheme="ColorScheme.Dark" />
        """;

    private const string Services = """
        builder.Services.AddIzzyBlazor();
        // ...
        app.MapIzzyBlazor();
        """;

    private const string LightDark = """
        .release-band {
          background: light-dark(#fff7ed, #2a1a0c);
          border-color: light-dark(#fed7aa, #7c2d12);
        }
        """;
}
